# Ignore rules for `docker build -f oauth/Dockerfile .`.
#
# BuildKit resolves `<dockerfile path>.dockerignore` in preference to the
# context's own `.dockerignore`, so this file — and not the root one — decides
# what reaches the OAuth build. That is the mechanism behind #126: both images
# now build from the repository root, the root `.dockerignore` still excludes
# `oauth` so the connector image never carries this package, and this file
# excludes the connector's tree so this image never carries that one.
#
# Neither file may exclude `shared` — it is the one directory both images
# compile.
#
# It replaces oauth/.dockerignore, which applied only while the build context
# was oauth/ and stopped being consulted the moment the context moved.

# --- never in any image -----------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store

# --- the connector's tree ---------------------------------------------------
# Its absence is what makes a stray `import "../src/…"` from oauth/src fail in
# the build rather than in production. The oauth/ build context used to provide
# that property; these lines provide it now.
src
test
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.test.json
package.json
package-lock.json
ecosystem.config.cjs
scripts

# --- this package's own non-runtime files -----------------------------------
oauth/test
oauth/tsconfig.test.json

# --- secrets and state ------------------------------------------------------
secrets
oauth-data
data
accounts.json
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- repository furniture ---------------------------------------------------
.github
docs
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.test.yml
CHANGELOG.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
README.md
LICENSE
